Corresponding source: the archive zim-0.77.2.tar.gz in this directory is the
complete source of the program as it is installed (the installer only unpacks it).
The same release is published at https://zim-wiki.org/downloads/zim-0.77.2.tar.gz
and its source repository is https://github.com/zim-desktop-wiki/zim-desktop-wiki
(tag 0.77.2). The sha256 of the archive is listed in SOURCE.json.

Third-party material carried inside the upstream archive keeps its own terms, which
the upstream files state: the S5 slide show template (public domain), the Tango
base icons mentioned in the plugin sources (public domain) and the translation
files (BSD).

Component notices are collected in LICENSES/. Upstream copyright and license text are retained; local launch and isolation scripts are described above. The official release archive is fetched and checksum-verified at build time; SOURCE.json records its exact URL and version.

The local launch.py and exec_guard.c add a kernel seccomp filter before the wiki starts. The wiki process denies external program execution, including commands from custom tools or plugins. A separate helper preserves notebook version control through fixed Git subcommands inside exchange paths; hooks, network protocols and further execution are disabled. These launcher files are separate from the unchanged upstream source archive.
